# Request-scoped DI on the server (docs/compiler/codegen.md §13,
# docs/compiler/server.md §5). Every request gets a fresh request container:
# `.app` services start from their initial state on every request and are
# shared by everything within it. `.server` services are one per server
# process (docs/design/29-server-streaming.md), so their state carries across
# requests.

### two services in one request share one .app instance
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/RequestVisits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### the next request gets a fresh .app instance
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/RequestVisits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### state never leaks from one request to the next, on any worker
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/RequestVisits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### a fourth request is still fresh
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/RequestVisits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### a .server service counts its first hit
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/ProcessHits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 1}

### a .server service is shared by the next request
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/ProcessHits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 2}

### a .server service is shared across workers of one process
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/ProcessHits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### request-scoped rpcs in between don't touch the process counter
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/RequestVisits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 3}

### the process counter continues
POST /scopes.counting.CounterProtocol/ProcessHits
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": 4}

### during SSR the load and the components share the request's instance
GET /counts
>>> 200
~ load counted 2
~ badge sees 2

### every component instance in the request sees the same state
GET /counts
>>> 200
!~ badge sees 0
!~ badge sees 4

### a second render starts from a fresh container
GET /counts
>>> 200
~ load counted 2
!~ load counted 4

### SSR state is not shared with rpcs of other requests
GET /counts
>>> 200
~ load counted 2
